Sonos doesn't show up as the in `dlna_dmr/manifest.json` uses on `deviceType`:
```
  "ssdp": [
    {
      "deviceType": "urn:schemas-upnp-org:device:MediaRenderer:1"
    },
    {
      "deviceType": "urn:schemas-upnp-org:device:MediaRenderer:2"
    },
    {
      "deviceType": "urn:schemas-upnp-org:device:MediaRenderer:3"
    }
  ],
```

When the media renderer device is an embedded device, the actual `deviceType` in `info_with_desc` (in `homeassistant.components.ssdp.Scanner._ssdp_listener_callback`) is for the root device, not the embedded device, thus the domain is not matched. It'll probably work when in `manifest.json`, `deviceType` is replaced by `st` (in case of searches) or `nt` (in case of advertisements.) I think `st`/search is more reliable. Or, perhaps there are other solutions (either on the hass side or on the `async-upnp-client` side?)
